<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<?xml-model href="https://www.tei-c.org/Vault/P5/4.12.0/xml/tei/custom/schema/relaxng/tei_odds.rng" type="application/xml" schematypens="http://relaxng.org/ns/structure/1.0"?>
<TEI xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
  <teiHeader>
    <fileDesc>
      <titleStmt>
        <title>poc_odds: TEI for authoring ODD, with nested models</title>
      </titleStmt>
      <publicationStmt>
        <p>Part of the ODD Rendering Compiler proof of concept. Its schema specification follows
          the TEI's <ident>tei_odds.odd</ident> (TEI P5 4.12.0, by Sebastian Rahtz, © TEI
          Consortium, CC BY 3.0 / BSD-2-Clause).</p>
      </publicationStmt>
      <sourceDesc>
        <p>Written for the nested page-break extension.</p>
      </sourceDesc>
    </fileDesc>
  </teiHeader>
  <text>
    <body>
      <p>The ODD language of TEI P5 4.12.0 (<ident>tei_odds</ident>), with one change: a
        <gi>model</gi> may hold a <gi>modelSequence</gi>, after its params and renditions. That is
        the nested model Boot (2024) proposes, where one model has several behaviours at once. In
        TEI a <gi>modelSequence</gi> stands only beside models, as an alternative to them.</p>
      <p>Compile it with the TEI Stylesheets (<ident>odd2odd</ident>, then <ident>odd2relax</ident>)
        and validate an ODD that uses nested models against the result; see
        <ident>validate.sh</ident>.</p>
      <schemaSpec ident="poc_odds" start="TEI schemaSpec elementSpec classSpec macroSpec div"
        source="https://www.tei-c.org/Vault/P5/4.12.0/xml/tei/odd/p5subset.xml">
        <moduleRef url="https://www.tei-c.org/Vault/P5/4.12.0/xml/tei/Exemplars/relaxng.rng"/>
        <moduleRef key="header"/>
        <moduleRef key="core"/>
        <moduleRef key="tei"/>
        <moduleRef key="gaiji"/>
        <moduleRef key="textstructure"/>
        <moduleRef key="tagdocs"/>
        <moduleRef key="dictionaries"/>
        <moduleRef key="linking"/>
        <moduleRef key="figures"/>
        <elementSpec ident="teiCorpus" mode="delete" module="core"/>
        <elementSpec ident="model" mode="change" module="tagdocs">
          <content>
            <sequence>
              <alternate minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
                <classRef key="model.identEquiv"/>
                <classRef key="model.descLike"/>
              </alternate>
              <elementRef key="param" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
              <elementRef key="outputRendition" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
              <elementRef key="modelSequence" minOccurs="0"/>
            </sequence>
          </content>
        </elementSpec>
      </schemaSpec>
    </body>
  </text>
</TEI>
